From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:32:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qosify: show each interface's ifb as the daemon reports it

qosify-status derives the name of an interface's ifb in a way of its
own: "ifb-" and the device's name, cut at sixteen characters. For a
device name of 12 to 15 characters that is no interface name at all,
and not the one the daemon gives the ifb, the name's first two
characters and its last nine.

Carry the qosify patch that reports each active interface's ifb in its
status, and have qosify-status show that device. It is meant for qosify
upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/network/config/qosify/Makefile        |  2 +-
 .../network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status |  6 ++--
 ...t-each-interface-s-ifb-in-its-status.patch | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 package/network/config/qosify/patches/104-interface-report-each-interface-s-ifb-in-its-status.patch

diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile b/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
index 2127f0e..0d3b431 100644
--- a/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_DATE:=2026-10-14
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=b3ee50eff9d924a6c7a0c02b9ab1afc6056b7a00
 PKG_MIRROR_HASH:=924dd93cfc3205da58127bbd0397322e0b48819be28db3538e6ab9fc6196c536
-PKG_RELEASE:=5
+PKG_RELEASE:=6
 
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0
 PKG_MAINTAINER:=Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status b/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status
index dc58232..0ff60d1 100644
--- a/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ dev_status() {
 }
 
 common_status() {
-	json_get_vars ifname ingress egress
+	json_get_vars ifname ingress egress ifb
 
 	[ -n "$ifname" ] || return
 
@@ -15,9 +15,9 @@ common_status() {
 		echo "egress status:"
 		dev_status "$ifname"
 	}
-	[ "$ingress" -gt 0 ] && {
+	[ -n "$ifb" ] && {
 		echo "ingress status:"
-		dev_status "$(printf %.16s "ifb-$ifname")"
+		dev_status "$ifb"
 	}
 }
 
diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/patches/104-interface-report-each-interface-s-ifb-in-its-status.patch b/package/network/config/qosify/patches/104-interface-report-each-interface-s-ifb-in-its-status.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d1565f9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/patches/104-interface-report-each-interface-s-ifb-in-its-status.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] interface: report each interface's ifb in its status
+
+Report the ifb that shapes an active interface's ingress in its status,
+as "ifb", so that a status tool can show the device the daemon created.
+qosify-status derives a name of its own, "ifb-" and the device's name
+cut at sixteen characters, which for a device name of 12 to 15
+characters is not the daemon's: that keeps the name's first two
+characters and its last nine.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+ interface.c | 2 ++
+ 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)
+
+diff --git a/interface.c b/interface.c
+index 2a673ea..170d83f 100644
+--- a/interface.c
++++ b/interface.c
+@@ -735,6 +735,8 @@ __qosify_iface_status(struct blob_buf *b, struct qosify_iface *iface)
+ 		blobmsg_add_string(b, "ifname", iface->ifname);
+ 	blobmsg_add_u8(b, "egress", iface->config.egress);
+ 	blobmsg_add_u8(b, "ingress", iface->config.ingress);
++	if (iface->active && iface->config.ingress)
++		blobmsg_add_string(b, "ifb", interface_ifb_name(iface));
+ 	blobmsg_close_table(b, c);
+ 
+ }
